---
import DocsLayout from "../_components/DocsLayout.bangala"
import CodeBlock from "../_components/CodeBlock.bangala"

const build = `npm run build
# upload dist/`;

const vercel = `npx bangala deploy vercel`;
const netlify = `npx bangala deploy netlify`;
const cloudflare = `npx bangala deploy cloudflare-pages`;
const github = `- name: Build site
  run: npx bangala build --out-dir dist

- name: Upload artifact
  uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3
  with:
    path: dist`;

const headings = [
  { id: "model", label: "Deployment model" },
  { id: "vercel", label: "Vercel" },
  { id: "netlify", label: "Netlify" },
  { id: "cloudflare", label: "Cloudflare Pages" },
  { id: "github-pages", label: "GitHub Pages" },
];
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Adapters | bangala.js"
  description="Deployer un site bangala.js sur Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages, GitHub Pages ou un host statique."
  path="/docs/adapters"
  section="Reference"
  lead="Bangala outputs static files. Adapters only write host config; there is no server runtime to deploy for the v1 static build."
  headings={headings}
  prev={{ href: "/docs/api", label: "API Reference" }}
  next={{ href: "/vs/nextjs", label: "Bangala vs Next.js" }}
>
  <h2 id="model">Deployment model</h2>
  <p>Run the build, then upload <code>dist/</code>. The generated HTML includes the client runtime only if islands are present and client injection is enabled.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="Terminal" lang="bash" code={build}/>

  <h2 id="vercel">Vercel</h2>
  <p>The Vercel adapter writes <code>vercel.json</code> with <code>npm run build</code> and <code>dist</code> as the output directory.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="Terminal" lang="bash" code={vercel}/>

  <h2 id="netlify">Netlify</h2>
  <p>The Netlify adapter writes <code>netlify.toml</code> with the build command, publish directory, and a safe content-type header.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="Terminal" lang="bash" code={netlify}/>

  <h2 id="cloudflare">Cloudflare Pages</h2>
  <p>The Cloudflare Pages adapter writes a minimal <code>wrangler.toml</code>. The aliases <code>cloudflare</code> and <code>cf-pages</code> are accepted.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="Terminal" lang="bash" code={cloudflare}/>

  <h2 id="github-pages">GitHub Pages</h2>
  <p>GitHub Pages does not need a dedicated adapter. Build the site and upload the generated directory as a Pages artifact.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename=".github/workflows/deploy.yml" lang="yaml" code={github}/>
</DocsLayout>
